From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ui/keyboard: keep the OSK populated when a level is missing

Three related defects, all reachable from a page that moves focus between a
normal text field and a tel/number field -- a phone-number login form in a
browser is the reported case.

1. _setActiveLevel() assigns layers[activeLevel] to _currentPage without
   checking that the layer exists. Purpose-specific layouts have a single
   level (phone.json only defines 'default'), so a stale 'shift' request sets
   _currentPage to undefined and the connect() right after it throws. That
   skips _updateCurrentPageVisible(), and since _updateLayout() hides every
   layer it built, the keyboard stays open while showing no keys at all.
2. _updateLevelFromHints() resolves the requested level asynchronously via
   'surrounding-text-set'. The handler outlives the layout it was registered
   for, so focusing a tel field afterwards asks for 'shift' in a layout that
   has no shift layer. Drop the pending request when the layout changes.
3. maybeHandleEvent() passes global.stage.get_event_actor() straight into
   keyboardBox.contains(), which throws "Argument descendant may not be null"
   whenever the event has no actor.

On Debian 13 arm64 this surfaced as 102 consecutive
"TypeError: this._currentPage is undefined" lines in the journal while a
phone number was being typed, with a keyboard that had no visible keys.

Applies to upstream GNOME Shell 48.7 (gnome-48 branch).
Debian 13 source: gnome-shell 48.7-0+deb13u2.
Origin: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-shell/-/blob/gnome-48/js/ui/keyboard.js
Forwarded: no
---
--- a/js/ui/keyboard.js
+++ b/js/ui/keyboard.js
@@ -1180,6 +1180,9 @@
 
         const actor = global.stage.get_event_actor(event);
 
+        if (!actor)
+            return false;
+
         if (Main.layoutManager.keyboardBox.contains(actor) ||
             !!actor._extendedKeys || !!actor.extendedKey) {
             actor.event(event, true);
@@ -1384,8 +1387,7 @@
                             this._setActiveLevel('default');
                     }
 
-                    Main.inputMethod.disconnect(this._surroundingTextId);
-                    this._surroundingTextId = 0;
+                    this._clearSurroundingTextRequest();
                 });
             Main.inputMethod.request_surrounding();
             return;
@@ -1395,6 +1397,14 @@
             this._setActiveLevel('default');
     }
 
+    _clearSurroundingTextRequest() {
+        if (!this._surroundingTextId)
+            return;
+
+        Main.inputMethod.disconnect(this._surroundingTextId);
+        this._surroundingTextId = 0;
+    }
+
     _onKeyFocusChanged() {
         let focus = global.stage.key_focus;
 
@@ -1421,6 +1431,13 @@
     }
 
     _updateLayout(groupName, purpose) {
+        // Hints-driven level changes are asynchronous: _updateLevelFromHints()
+        // registers a surrounding-text handler and the level it asks for is only
+        // resolved later, against whatever layout is current by then. Drop any
+        // pending request first -- the level it wants may not exist in the new
+        // layout (phone.json defines a single 'default' level, no 'shift').
+        this._clearSurroundingTextRequest();
+
         let keyboardModel = null;
         let layers = {};
         let layout = new Clutter.Actor({
@@ -1706,6 +1723,15 @@
         const layers = this._layers;
         let currentPage = layers[activeLevel];
 
+        // The requested level is not part of the layout that is currently in
+        // use. The purpose-specific layouts are the usual case: phone.json
+        // only defines 'default', so any stale 'shift' request lands here.
+        // Bail out before assigning undefined to _currentPage -- the connect()
+        // below would throw, skipping _updateCurrentPageVisible(), and every
+        // layer stays hidden: the keyboard is open but shows no keys at all.
+        if (!currentPage)
+            return;
+
         if (this._currentPage === currentPage) {
             this._updateCurrentPageVisible();
             return;
